[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2160","id":4835601213,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT-9fds8AAAABIDlrPQ","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2160","diff_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2160.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2160.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2160","number":2160,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(ci-ratchet): read the window's run association from workflow_run.id; re-record the cold-start baseline","user":{"login":"hpo-author[bot]","id":331381602,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOE8B7Yg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/hpo-author","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The new ci-ratchet job went red on its first main grade: its \"recent window\"\nwas never a window, and the re-record below pays the cold start against the\nfixed gather, not the broken one.\n\n## Head\n\n71626afbe\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nThe gather fix is a jq selection, so the mutation is the old expression: against\nthe live artifacts API (per_page 100, 2026-10-12), the old\n`select(.run_id != GITHUB_RUN_ID)` admits all 21 ci-metrics candidates of run\n38302634903 (null passes `!=`; every artifact's `run_id` is now null), and its\n`unique_by(.run, .name)` over null collapses the window to 3 artifacts with\n`run: null`. The fixed `(.workflow_run.id // .run_id // 0)` selection admits\n**0** of the run's own artifacts and dedups over 9 distinct real run ids.\nGrading a window dir replanted with the run's own closures artifact (what the\nbroken gather downloaded as `w11775150319-*`) derives `script_runs_per_push`\n96 -- the red reproduced; the fixed-gather dir derives 63. Both probes are the\ntool's own `read_metrics`/`script_runs` under `tests/ci_ratchet.py`.\n\n## Null control\n\nThe unmodified tree (81acae2b7) is the red itself: job 115016595648,\n`GREW script_runs_per_push: 96 (budget 53)`, and grading the same run's\nartifacts through a shifted window derives 63, not 96 -- the null control is\nwhat showed the grade was not a property of the tree.\n\n## Figures\n\n- old selection admits the run's own artifacts: `gh api repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/actions/artifacts?per_page=100 --jq '[.artifacts[] | select(.name | startswith(\"ci-metrics-\")) | select(.expired == false) | select(.run_id != (38302634903 | tonumber))] | length'` -> 21\n- fixed selection admits none: same query with `select((.workflow_run.id // .run_id // 0) != (38302634903 | tonumber))` intersected with `== 38302634903` -> 0\n- planted duplicate double-count: `python3 -c` over `tests/ci_ratchet.py read_metrics/script_runs`, dirs `seat/dup_probe` vs `seat/fixed_metrics` -> 96 vs 63\n- re-record: `python3 tests/ci_ratchet.py --metrics-dir seat/fixed_metrics --runs-json seat/runs.json --record \"...\"` -> `recorded 20 metric(s) at 81acae2b732b`\n\nMetric provenance (each from the fixed selection's derivation): `script_runs_per_push 63` = the push run's own closures 33 + coverage 20 + fast-lane probe 10 rows; `script_runs_full_case_pr 63` = pull_request run 38293720450, fast mode full, 63 closures+coverage rows (the window's most expensive full-case PR); `critical_path_minutes 54.825` = median of the 8 completed push Tests runs (`gh api repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/actions/workflows/tests.yml/runs?event=push&branch=main&per_page=8`); all 17 `archscore.*` rows unchanged at 81acae2b7.\n\n## Red checks\n\nTests on main, run 38302634903, job ci-ratchet 115016595648: `GREW\nscript_runs_per_push 96 (budget 53)`. Cause: the artifacts-list API stopped\nreturning `run_id` (upstream API shape change), so the window query's\nself-exclusion and per-run dedup both silently read null -- this run's own\nlanes leaked into the \"recent window\" and double-counted. Cheaper detector: no\nstatic one exists for a remote API's response shape; the ratchet's own\nreproducibility is the detector, and this PR's probe (derive the same run's\ngrade under a shifted window) is the standing cheap check -- a grade that moves\nwhen only the window moved indicts the gather, not the tree. The cold start\nitself is one-shot: no honest baseline existed to grade against, so the\ndeliberate `--record` is the countermeasure and pays it once.\n\n`budget-raise-gate` is red on this head and stays red until tvofi approves at\nit (mandate 6126981155; no review is posted by this seat): two caps went up,\n`script_runs_per_push` 53 -> 63 and `script_runs_full_case_pr` 53 -> 63, both\nraises the measurement, not a loosening of an un-grown metric -- 53 was an\nanalytic fail-closed estimate written before any run had emitted artifacts\n(2132's own reason field says so), and every other recorded value held or\ntightened (`critical_path_minutes` 61.0 -> 54.825, archscore unchanged).\nCheaper detector for the gate itself: none -- the one-approving-review rule at\nthe raise's head is the owner's own budget-raise gate (0013).\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone\n\n## Friction\n\nnone\n","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:14:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T14:59:34Z","clos